{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt the scope for a candidate outcome-map design note. Hugh asked planner to turn the reviewed local mock-up into a durable note and ask Claude to review it. The note will specify a horizontal, zoomable, thread-level graph beside the existing table presentation; draw only recorded provenance, ratification and supersession relations; keep board populations and search outside the graph; show recorded waits-on parties on cards; open the existing full-width thread view without squeezing it into the selection rail; preserve stable deterministic layout; and state plainly what the current data cannot prove about blockage. This proposal authorizes the note, not the UI implementation.","body":{"conditions":"Planner publishes notes/2026-08-30-outcome-map.md from a separate request/* worktree, based on the live UI artifact. The note records the agreed graph semantics, interactions, visual channels, actionability limits, stability and accessibility invariants, and the optional future work-class vocabulary. After publishing the exact-head artifact, planner files and obtains ratification of an adoption proposal for that artifact, then requests independent design review from Claude resting on both the artifact and ratified adoption proposal. No UI source change is authorized by this proposal."}}